  "baseline": [],
  "env": [
    {
      "name": "PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE",
      "value": "1",
      "notes": "node-gyp ships gyp/pylib and CPython writes __pycache__/*.pyc beside any module it imports. The jail refuses correctly and the build succeeds either way, because bytecode is a pure cache — but the refused writes were counted as side effects and made nine native packages (keccak, lz4, ssh2, ...) demand write.userHome, the second-widest grant, when bytecode was the ENTIRE delta between arms. Setting this stops the write happening at all, which is the general fix; the harness previously filtered .pyc after the fact, which is the same fix re-derived per tool."
    }
  ]
}
